# js-vtt

TypeScript library for parsing, building, and manipulating WebVTT (and SRT) subtitle files. Pure ESM (`"type": "module"`). Package manager: **pnpm**.

## Layout

- `src/` — library source; public entry is `src/index.ts`
- `src/vtt.ts` — core `VTT` class
- `src/segments/` — `Segment` hierarchy (Header, Cue, Region, Style, Comment)
- `src/errors/` — typed error classes (default exports, re-exported from index)
- `src/helpers.ts` — segment/format detectors
- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests mirroring `src/`
- `docs/` — VitePress documentation
- Use `src/main.ts` only as a local scratch/dev entry; do not ship it

## Commands

```bash
pnpm test      # vitest + coverage
pnpm lint      # eslint
pnpm build     # tsdown → dist/
pnpm format    # prettier
pnpm changeset # versioning before release
```

## Non-negotiables

- Keep the package **ESM-only** (no CommonJS)
- Prefer extending existing segment / error patterns over new abstractions
- Do not break the public API (`VTT`, segments, helpers, errors) without a changeset and docs/readme updates
- Prefer `pnpm` over npm/yarn in scripts and docs examples when adding project-local instructions
